.TH FORAGE "1" "2026\-05\-17" "anythingllm\-feeder 0.1.8" "Generated Python Manual"
.SH NAME
forage \- Extract documents and videos to Markdown, organized as named collections of sources.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forage
[-h] [--version] [-v] [-q] [--json] [--print-completion {bash,zsh,tcsh}] {create,list,info,update,transcribe,repair,add-source,remove-source,set-source,rename,remove,purge,doctor,install-extras} ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.SS \fBforage create\fR
create a new collection

usage: forage create [\-h] \-\-source NAME=PATH [\-v] [\-q] [\-\-json] name

arguments:
.RS 7
.TP
\fBname\fR
.RE


options:
.RS 7
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI\,NAME=PATH\/\fR
add a named source (repeatable, at least one required)

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR

.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
machine\-readable JSON output where applicable
.RE

